  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THRIVING COMMUNITIES THROUGH WOMEN&apos;S ECONOMIC EMPOWERMENT, IMPROVED CLIMATE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of the project is to empower vulnerable people in two regions within Ethiopia (Oromia and Southern Nations, Nationalities and Peoples) to lift themselves out of poverty through climate adaptive agriculture, business development and establishing civil society organisations. Ethiopia has high levels of multidimensional poverty, further impacted by continued economic stresses, the impact of conflict in Northern Ethiopia and prolonged drought in the southeast of the country. Women, girls and people with disabilities are disproportionality affected by chronic poverty, with few opportunities to organise themselves and establish a public voice.</narrative>
  </description>
